From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:31:12 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: qcom: allow HS-G3 at 150 MHz on pre-v4 controllers

ufs_qcom_freq_to_gear_speed() maps a 150 MHz UniPro core clock to
HS-G2. That holds for the newer controllers whose OPP tables go up to
300 or 403 MHz. On v3 controllers, however, 150 MHz is the highest
UniPro rate, and these controllers run HS-G3 at it.

Before commit c02fe9e222d1 ("scsi: ufs: qcom: Implement the
freq_to_gear_speed() vop"), scaling up restored the power mode that was
negotiated at probe. Since that commit, the gear comes from the UniPro
rate, so a link that negotiated HS-G3 is scaled down to HS-G2 at its
highest OPP and stays there under load. On the comma four (SDM845,
SanDisk SDINDDH4 UFS 2.1), sequential O_DIRECT reads drop to 517 MB/s,
compared to 725 MB/s on the downstream kernel, which runs HS-G3 Rate B
at a 150 MHz UniPro clock.

Map 150 MHz to HS-G3 on controllers older than v4. Their maximum gear
is HS-G3 anyway (see ufs_qcom_get_hs_gear()), and the result is still
capped by the negotiated gear. With this change, the SDM845 link runs
HS-G3 Rate B under load and reads reach 744-779 MB/s.

Other affected platforms: SM6350 and QCS615 also top out at a 150 MHz
UniPro OPP, and if their controllers are older than v4, they also go
from HS-G2 to HS-G3 at that OPP. I tested only SDM845. Controllers on
v4 and later, where 150 MHz is an intermediate OPP (SC7280, SM8550 and
others), keep HS-G2.

Fixes: c02fe9e222d1 ("scsi: ufs: qcom: Implement the freq_to_gear_speed() vop")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org # 6.15+
Signed-off-by: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
---
 drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
index 954be9343f..89a3ca0657 100644
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -2497,6 +2497,7 @@ static unsigned long ufs_qcom_opp_freq_to_clk_freq(struct ufs_hba *hba,
 
 static u32 ufs_qcom_freq_to_gear_speed(struct ufs_hba *hba, unsigned long freq)
 {
+	struct ufs_qcom_host *host = ufshcd_get_variant(hba);
 	u32 gear = UFS_HS_DONT_CHANGE;
 	unsigned long unipro_freq;
 
@@ -2515,6 +2516,12 @@ static u32 ufs_qcom_freq_to_gear_speed(struct ufs_hba *hba, unsigned long freq)
 		gear = UFS_HS_G3;
 		break;
 	case 150000000:
+		/*
+		 * Controllers older than v4 top out at a 150 MHz UniPro core
+		 * clock, and run HS-G3 at that rate.
+		 */
+		gear = host->hw_ver.major < 0x4 ? UFS_HS_G3 : UFS_HS_G2;
+		break;
 	case 100000000:
 		gear = UFS_HS_G2;
 		break;
